WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:02.712
(whooshing)

00:00:15.189 --> 00:00:17.522
- [Narrator] "Better than
a thousand hollow words,

00:00:17.522 --> 00:00:19.272
is one word", Buddha.

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:22.532
I'm going to share a secret with you,

00:00:22.532 --> 00:00:25.443
a secret so powerful that
once you discover it,

00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:27.475
every decision you make in your life

00:00:27.475 --> 00:00:30.011
and business will become easier.

00:00:30.011 --> 00:00:32.227
Doors will start to open
where before you struggled

00:00:32.227 --> 00:00:33.962
to make any progress.

00:00:33.962 --> 00:00:35.162
You'll finally feel like you're

00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:37.267
living your life with a purpose

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.338
instead of fighting the world around you.

00:00:40.338 --> 00:00:41.737
Great leaders have used this secret

00:00:41.737 --> 00:00:44.809
to build powerful companies,
spark important movements,

00:00:44.809 --> 00:00:47.018
and create meaningful change.

00:00:47.018 --> 00:00:49.462
And now you can too.

00:00:49.462 --> 00:00:51.038
Here's the secret,

00:00:51.038 --> 00:00:54.221
there is one word that
defines who you are.

00:00:54.221 --> 00:00:56.450
There is one word that
connects all the things

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.114
in your life that make you come alive.

00:00:59.114 --> 00:01:01.809
Think about the friends you
have, the music you listen to,

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:04.313
the books you read, the movies you watch,

00:01:04.313 --> 00:01:05.898
the companies you've worked for,

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.466
the businesses you've started.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:08.896
Think about everything in your life

00:01:08.896 --> 00:01:11.416
right now that you enjoy.

00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:13.464
They're all connected.

00:01:13.464 --> 00:01:15.975
Until you figure out
what that connection is,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.543
you'll never live up to your potential.

00:01:18.543 --> 00:01:20.079
What's your favorite song

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:22.040
and what does it have to do
with who your best friend

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.910
or favorite book is?

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.158
The answer is everything.

00:01:26.158 --> 00:01:30.997
And it can be boiled down to
one simple, powerful word.

00:01:30.997 --> 00:01:33.765
Great people can be described in one word.

00:01:33.765 --> 00:01:36.174
Martin Luther King, Jr., equality.

00:01:36.174 --> 00:01:38.092
Oprah Winfrey, heart.

00:01:38.092 --> 00:01:39.675
Steve Jobs, impact.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.548
How 'about you?

00:01:42.548 --> 00:01:45.371
If you want to break free
from the chains of mediocrity

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.158
and really make an impact,

00:01:47.158 --> 00:01:50.011
then it starts with finding your one word.

00:01:50.011 --> 00:01:54.178
You have to stand for something
powerful and important.

00:01:58.578 --> 00:02:00.911
(whooshing)

